            <ArticleTitle>A case of hyoscine-related oesophagitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>650-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a previously unreported association between hyoscine hydrobromide and severe oesophagitis, with ulceration visible almost to the submucosa in the distal oesophagus. The condition resolved with cessation of tablets and 2 months' treatment with a proton-pump inhibitor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
